// Hale stdlib — std::law: the standard constitutions a program or an
// environment adopts without importing anything (`hale check --adopt
// std::law::Standard`, `[environments.<env>] constitution =
// "std::law::Standard"`). Loaded only when one is adopted, so a program
// that adopts none pays nothing.

// The standard practices' law (#1591). A served or attached program
// writes to the terminal only through its logger: nothing it declares
// reaches a write to standard output or standard error except through
// `std::log`'s sinks.
constitution Standard {
    logs_structured: forbid reaches(program, effects(stdio)) avoiding std::log::*;
}
